The '''1984 African Cup of Nations''' was the 14th edition of the [[Africa Cup of Nations]], the [[association football|football]] championship of Africa ([[Confederation of African Football|CAF]]). It was hosted by Ivory Coast. Just like in [[1982 African Cup of Nations|1982]], the field of eight teams was split into two groups of four. [[Cameroon national football team|Cameroon]] won its first championship, beating [[Nigeria national football team|Nigeria]] in the final 3−1.

